      "description": "Watch Gornik Zabrze vs Ferencváros highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 13, 2026. The stage was set for a compelling UEFA Europa League encounter on August 13, 2026, as Gornik Zabrze hosted Ferencváros in a clash of tactical discipline. Both sides entered the pitch with high ambitions, looking to establish momentum in a match that promised to be decided by the narrowest of margins. Urbanski Strikes from the Spot The opening stages of the game were characterized by a fierce physical battle, particularly in the midfield. Ferencváros struggled to keep their composure under pressure, leading to an early yellow card for Attila Osvath in the 26th minute. As the first half drew to a close, the intensity spiked. A foul by Philippe Rommens in the 44th minute earned him a booking and, more importantly, handed the hosts a golden opportunity. Kacper Urbanski stepped up to the penalty spot in the 45th minute and coolly converted, sending the home crowd into raptures and giving Gornik Zabrze a vital lead at the break. Defensive Calamity Seals the Result The second half saw Ferencváros attempt to claw their way back into the contest with a series of tactical changes. The introduction of Naby Keita and Adam Nagy around the hour mark was intended to spark creativity, but the Gornik Zabrze backline remained resilient. The match reached its turning point in the 82nd minute when a moment of misfortune struck the visitors. Michal Sacek inadvertently directed the ball into his own net, gifting Gornik Zabrze a two-goal cushion that felt insurmountable given the flow of the game. In the closing stages, both managers utilized their benches to manage the final minutes. Gornik Zabrze brought on fresh legs in Ondrej Zmrzly and Yvan Ikia Dimi to see out the result, while Ferencváros made late attacking throws with Kenan Kodro and Nathan Zohore . After five minutes of added time, the referee blew the final whistle, confirming a professional and clinical victory for the Polish side on their home turf."
